<title>FRANCE: Juppe plans to cut charges on low wages - paper.</title>
<headline>Juppe plans to cut charges on low wages - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Alain Juppe plans a new reduction of the social charges on low wages in 1998 which would cost the state between four and six billion francs, financed by savings on job creation subsidies, a newspaper said.</p>
<p>The La Tribune Desfosses said in its Thursday edition that the plan would be presented to the European Commission in the next week.</p>
<p>The paper said the charge reduction would be between 1,168 and 2,200 francs for someone on the level of the Smic minimum wage.</p>
</text>
